   "subject": "Adaptive parallel tempering in NIMBLE",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>This has already been discussed in the <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/nimble-users/d9QxpgvSovE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/%23!topic/nimble-users/d9QxpgvSovE&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792477140015000&amp;usg=AOvVaw00sfNOTSeACbBvpM6vIpO2\">exchanges between chains in Nimble</a> thread - I&#39;m just re-posting here for greater visibility.<br></div><div><br></div><div>A set of nimble functions for adaptive parallel tempering are available in a small library called NimbleSnippets available <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.1049549\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.1049549&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792477140015000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2YMIr-bAQrkkLX8Mn1_vDC\">here</a>. The source code can be built into an R package and installed using </div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"></blockquote><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\"><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span>cd path</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">/</span><span>to</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">/</span><span>nimble</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">-</span><span>snippets<br>R CMD build nimble</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">-</span><span>snippets<br>R CMD INSTALL </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">NimbleSnippets_1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">0.1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">.</span><span>tar</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">.</span><span>gz</span></div></code></div></span></div></code></div><br>Feel free to contact me if you have any difficulties, or successes, with the package.<div><br></div><div>Best</div><div>David<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"></blockquote><div><br></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "5eoQdRv3AQAJ",
   "from": "David Pleydell",
