   "date": "2020-09-04T11:38:21Z",
   "subject": "Re: Adaptive parallel tempering in NIMBLE",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div>Dear nimble users</div><div><br></div><div>Some news concerning the adaptive parallel tempering package. <br></div><div>- The package name has been changed to nimbleAPT.</div><div>- Version 1.0.3 has been released.</div><div>- Minor updates for compatibility with developments in nimble are included.</div><div>- A vignette has been added demonstrating how to sample multi-modal posteriors using APT versions of nimble&#39;s samplers.</div><div>- Installation instructions are available here <a href=\"https://github.com/DRJP/nimbleAPT\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/DRJP/nimbleAPT&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792477140016000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2dHsaBYwNOBvrpNNWVCig6\">https://github.com/DRJP/nimbleAPT</a></div><div>- Citation details are available here <a href=\"https://zenodo.org/record/1049549#.X1ImKHVfikA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://zenodo.org/record/1049549%23.X1ImKHVfikA&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792477140016000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3ep0vrTtfZXgaquD8Br_-Z\">https://zenodo.org/record/1049549#.X1ImKHVfikA</a><br><br></div><div>Cheers</div><div>David</div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div><br></div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Wednesday, 15 November 2017 at 11:51:21 UTC+1 David Pleydell wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>This has already been discussed in the <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/nimble-users/d9QxpgvSovE\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/%23!topic/nimble-users/d9QxpgvSovE&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792477140016000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3GCZVZQ89wukvp0GelT4gk\">exchanges between chains in Nimble</a> thread - I&#39;m just re-posting here for greater visibility.<br></div><div><br></div><div>A set of nimble functions for adaptive parallel tempering are available in a small library called NimbleSnippets available <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.1049549\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.1049549&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792477140016000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2V_msOPeCWEwVbi6bAx_OO\">here</a>. The source code can be built into an R package and installed using </div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"></blockquote><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\"><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span>cd path</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">/</span><span>to</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">/</span><span>nimble</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">-</span><span>snippets<br>R CMD build nimble</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">-</span><span>snippets<br>R CMD INSTALL </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">NimbleSnippets_1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">0.1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">.</span><span>tar</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">.</span><span>gz</span></div></code></div></span></div></code></div><br>Feel free to contact me if you have any difficulties, or successes, with the package.<div><br></div><div>Best</div><div>David<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"></blockquote><div><br></div></div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ]
   ]
